WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:18,210
taking Iverbectin and I'm up to 120 milligrams daily. Remember that the dose for Iverbectin for cancer

00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:24,450
would be a half a milligram per kilogram weight. So you convert your weight into kilograms,

00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:31,570
you start at a half a milligram per kilogram of your weight, and then you could slowly titrate

00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:37,810
up from there. The past week since I've increased the dose, I've had extra severe brain fog

00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:43,170
and my memory is greatly impacted as well. Could these be side effects of the Iverbectin?

00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:51,330
Should I cut back? And how slowly should I increase again? So could these be side effects of

00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:58,930
the Iverbectin? Yes, they could be. Should you cut back? Yeah, probably. Should you go back up

00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:06,530
again? Well, it's good. It depends on where you're at with your cancer. If your answer to that question

00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:12,050
is, well, my cancer is pretty stable. I don't think it's growing. There's no other, there's no

00:01:13,570 --> 00:01:19,250
subjective signs that it's growing. There's no objective signs that it's growing with different

00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:26,050
blood tests with PET scans, with CT scans, with tumor markers. Then I wouldn't necessarily

00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:32,450
raise my dose. Matter of fact, you might want to lower your dose. If there is subjective and or

00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:38,370
objective signs that the cancer is going in the wrong direction that it's growing, then yes,

00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:44,530
then maybe you slowly go back up. Cut back on your dose. See if those symptoms go away and then you

00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:55,250
could go up slowly. So that's how I would at least approach that.

